# CBIM project

CBIM provides optional, user-invoked Skills for project knowledge, code, architecture, development, and explicit memory management.

Use normal Claude Code behavior unless a CBIM Skill matches the request. Skills run in the main conversation; they do not dispatch agents, run behavior trees, schedule background work, or capture memory automatically.

Memory is changed only when the user explicitly asks to create, inspect, query, update, delete, or reindex it. Follow normal host permissions and preserve project files and user configuration.
